{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cf2U2meePoUjPt3jdNecF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have all necessary files. Let me evaluate each challenged id against the bounded evidence.\n\n**production-path** — `run.py::main()` calls `build_agent()` and passes the agent to `converse()`, which routes `if agent is not None:` to `ask(agent, deps, ...)` (legacy PydanticAI tool loop). `plan_and_execute()` is only reached via the `agent is None` pipeline branch. Confirmed.\n\n**bad-request-origin** — The spec error boundary (`bad_request` = repairable incl. directory-identity), OD-03 (release-derived non-match → empty/partial success), and golden case `answer/VC-POC-01-empty` (99999 → empty success) support the origin separation. Confirmed.\n\n**request-validation** — The resolution asserts \"All per-question v0.3 request schemas are present in the permitted, hash-pinned repository inventory.\" But neither the permitted file inventory nor the dependency evidence contains any per-question request schema file (only `_index.json`, which lists references/materiality, not schema bodies with `additionalProperties`, nested keys, cardinality, conditionals, formats). The prior plan state explicitly said only VC-POC-01/03/04 schemas were supplied; the amendment reverses this without traced schema evidence. **Insufficient.**\n\n**static-vocabulary** — Registry `metric_lists`, input-catalog `x-poc-request-field-to-catalog-list` + embedded static enums, and the pinned snapshot are all present in the inventory. Confirmed.\n\n**typed-outcomes** — Ambiguous/zero-match directory outcomes and unnormalizable-selector clarification are grounded in the current planner (first-match) and present static vocabularies/directory behaviour. Confirmed.\n\n**filter-constraints** — VC-POC-09/10 \"at least one explicit filter\" is registry-enforced (constraints arrays; spec OD-07); closed `peer_filter_keys`/`segment_filter_keys` in the input-catalog schema support unknown-key rejection; verification names both tests. Confirmed.\n\n**nonvacuous-tests** — The after-Verification and contract `focused-nonvacuous-acceptance` use explicit node IDs, replacing `-k` substring selection so a missing/renamed test fails collection. Confirmed.\n\n**conditional-scope** — Scope expansion (run.py + test_run_cli.py) is contingent on production-path, which is confirmed; the legacy loop is left unchanged. Confirmed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97085,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97085},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2feaccea-09d8-4fe3-a5ee-c4eb883759f1","uuid":"ac4cdd8e-c8d1-4b11-a5d6-608c0e23b20d","request_id":"req_011Cf2U2kjq7Rb8cVQ6tpjtQ"}
