{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011Cf2U2meePoUjPt3jdNecF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01ERxrKvd7ZdfYVLNuwQDRZg","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"packet_sha256\":\"3c4725d5ade7543efec0bf0296bacccfdbebbec865f1c325b3bbfa05ad99a2a5\",\"findings\":[{\"id\":\"production-path\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"run.py::main() builds an agent via build_agent() and passes it to converse(), which routes 'if agent is not None' to ask(agent, deps, ...), i.e. the legacy PydanticAI tool loop; plan_and_execute() is reachable only via the agent-None pipeline branch. The amendment's minimal run.py wiring to pass None while retaining explicit-agent callers is consistent with the traced code.\"},{\"id\":\"bad-request-origin\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"The spec error boundary (bad_request repairable incl. absent directory identity), OD-03 (well-typed release-derived/open non-match yields empty/partial success, never bad_request), and golden case answer/VC-POC-01-empty (id 99999 -> empty success) support the origin separation: planner/schema defects and unexpected post-validation bad_request are operational, user-correctable selector/identity problems clarify, and valid non-matches remain successful.\"},{\"id\":\"request-validation\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"reason\":\"The resolution asserts all per-question v0.3 request schemas are present in the permitted, hash-pinned inventory, but neither the permitted file inventory nor the dependency evidence contains any per-question request-schema file. Only _index.json is present, giving filenames and materiality but not the schema bodies (additionalProperties, nested keys, types, cardinality, conditionals, formats). The prior plan state recorded that only VC-POC-01/03/04 schemas were supplied; the reversal to 'complete schema set present' is unverifiable from this bounded evidence, so complete pre-dispatch validation cannot be confirmed.\"},{\"id\":\"static-vocabulary\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"Deterministic pinned authorities are all present in the inventory: the registry metric_lists (profile_metrics, student_context_metrics), the input-catalog schema's x-poc-request-field-to-catalog-list mapping (including VC-POC-03.ratios and VC-POC-11.metrics) plus embedded static enums, and the captured snapshot as a baseline. No runtime emitter call is needed for these contract-static vocabularies.\"},{\"id\":\"typed-outcomes\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"The named scope (ambiguous schools and unnormalizable metrics) is grounded: the current planner's first-match resolution is visible and the proposed exactly-one-match rule yields ClarificationNeeded for zero/multiple matches, and unnormalizable selectors clarify against the present static vocabularies; conflicting identities raise TerminalError. Outcomes are typed clarification/TerminalError, none becoming Unsupported.\"},{\"id\":\"filter-constraints\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"VC-POC-09/10 'at least one explicit cohort-defining filter' is registry-declared (constraints arrays; VC-POC-09 sector default Catholic/Independent) and spec OD-07 keeps it registry/emitter-enforced; the closed peer_filter_keys and segment_filter_keys enums in the input-catalog schema support unknown-nested-key rejection. Verification names test_peer_filters_require_explicit_nondefault_filter and test_segment_filters_reject_unknown_nested_key.\"},{\"id\":\"nonvacuous-tests\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"The after-Verification approach and the contract's focused-nonvacuous-acceptance step use explicit pytest node IDs (module::test_name) rather than -k substring selection, so a renamed or absent test causes collection failure instead of a vacuous pass.\"},{\"id\":\"conditional-scope\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"Scope expansion is contingent on production-path, which the traced run.py/converse code confirms defaults to the legacy loop. The amendment adds only the minimal run.py wiring and a CLI regression test while leaving the legacy tool loop, its repair ceiling, and contract.material_inputs_for()/O-8 xfail unchanged, so the conditional expansion is justified.\"}]}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":97085,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":97085},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2feaccea-09d8-4fe3-a5ee-c4eb883759f1","uuid":"9ec3f4c3-df50-4dc9-a690-f69c868d621e","request_id":"req_011Cf2U2kjq7Rb8cVQ6tpjtQ"}
