r/identity problems clarify, and valid non-matches remain successful.\"},{\"id\":\"request-validation\",\"status\":\"unresolved\",\"reason\":\"The resolution asserts all per-question v0.3 request schemas are present in the permitted, hash-pinned inventory, but neither the permitted file inventory nor the dependency evidence contains any per-question request-schema file. Only _index.json is present, giving filenames and materiality but not the schema bodies (additionalProperties, nested keys, types, cardinality, conditionals, formats). The prior plan state recorded that only VC-POC-01/03/04 schemas were supplied; the reversal to 'complete schema set present' is unverifiable from this bounded evidence, so complete pre-dispatch validation cannot be confirmed.\"},{\"id\":\"static-vocabulary\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"Deterministic pinned authorities are all present in the inventory: the registry metric_lists (profile_metrics, student_context_metrics), the input-catalog schema's x-poc-request-field-to-catalog-list mapping (including VC-POC-03.ratios and VC-POC-11.metrics) plus embedded static enums, and the captured snapshot as a baseline. No runtime emitter call is needed for these contract-static vocabularies.\"},{\"id\":\"typed-outcomes\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"The named scope (ambiguous schools and unnormalizable metrics) is grounded: the current planner's first-match resolution is visible and the proposed exactly-one-match rule yields ClarificationNeeded for zero/multiple matches, and unnormalizable selectors clarify against the present static vocabularies; conflicting identities raise TerminalError. Outcomes are typed clarification/TerminalError, none becoming Unsupported.\"},{\"id\":\"filter-constraints\",\"status\":\"resolved\",\"reason\":\"VC-POC-09/10 'at least one explicit cohort-defining filter' is registry-declared (constraints arrays; VC-POC-09 sector default Catholic/Independent) and spec OD-07 keeps it registry/emitter-enforced; 